    # Execute pipeline as background job, then immediately wait & report Done (mirrors observed behavior before next pipeline/list item)
    # We fork a job child for multiple commands / external, but for single external we run it as job
    # Use normal pipeline execution but in a forked child? That would cause Done after all outputs; for single external original waits it and prints Done after.
    # Approach: spawn pipeline processes via parallel spawn logic in this process and wait, then print Done.
    # Simplest: fork a child that executes the pipeline (non-bg) and exits; parent waits, prints Done, $! = child pid if single external else child pid
    pid = os.fork()
